Debug this error: TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'map')

Code:
```
function UserList({ users }) {
  return (
    <ul>
      {users.map(user => (
        <li key={user.id}>{user.name}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}
```

## Error Analysis

**Error Message:**
```
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'map')
```

**Problematic Code:**
```
function UserList({ users }) {
  return (
    <ul>
      {users.map(user => (
        <li key={user.id}>{user.name}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}
```

## Root Cause
The error occurs because `users` is undefined when the component first renders.

## Fixed Code
```
function UserList({ users = [] }) {
  if (!users || users.length === 0) {
    return <p>No users found</p>;
  }

  return (
    <ul>
      {users.map(user => (
        <li key={user.id}>{user.name}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  );
}
```

## Key Learning Points
- Always provide default values for props that might be undefined
- Add null checks before calling array methods
- Consider loading states for async data

## Prevention Tips
1. Add proper error handling from the start
2. Write unit tests for edge cases
3. Use TypeScript/type hints for early error detection
4. Add defensive checks for external data

